  "system": {
    "description": {
      "type": "String",
      "label": "Description",
      "value": "<p>The arrow rips through your upper thigh, tearing through flesh and muscle, clipping the femoral artery before lodging in the femur bone itself. Blood starts spurting and you begin to feel distinctly inconvenienced.</p><p><strong>Effects:</strong> Gain @Condition[Bleeding] (3). Also, suffer a @UUID[Compendium.wfrp4e-core.items.Item.3S4OYOZLauXctmev]{Torn Muscle (Major)}. If you fail a <strong>Challenging (+0) Endurance</strong> Test you’re also unlucky enough to have had the artery severed high enough that an ordinary tourniquet is useless, in which case Surgery (and a long clamp) is necessary to remove the @Condition[Bleeding] Condition. </p><p><strong>Surgery (Hard)</strong> is required for Extraction.</p>"
    },
